1
00:00:03,265 --> 00:00:04,975
Damn, it's pouring.

2
00:00:05,976 --> 00:00:09,563
I'm cold. I'm so gonna get sick.

3
00:00:09,646 --> 00:00:11,565
Maybe I should just go home.

4
00:00:11,648 --> 00:00:13,483
But what about that awful thing?

5
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:16,611
ROACHES ARE UNSEEMLY,
SO INSTEAD, CAKE! YOU'RE WELCOME!

6
00:00:22,325 --> 00:00:23,160
Huh?

7
00:00:28,874 --> 00:00:29,708
Hmm.

8
00:00:31,626 --> 00:00:32,544
Uh…

9
00:00:33,336 --> 00:00:34,171
Oh, crap.

10
00:00:39,259 --> 00:00:40,343
Hey.

11
00:00:41,386 --> 00:00:43,180
Are you a runaway?

12
00:00:43,263 --> 00:00:44,431
No.

13
00:00:45,807 --> 00:00:48,101
No judgments,
you need to stay dry out here,

14
00:00:48,185 --> 00:00:51,730
but you do know there's been reports
of a creep in the park the last few days?

15
00:00:51,813 --> 00:00:53,732
What? No way!

16
00:00:56,902 --> 00:00:58,320
-Thanks for the head-ups.
-Huh?

17
00:00:58,403 --> 00:00:59,821
Uh, hey, wait.

18
00:01:01,907 --> 00:01:03,492
Keep your hands off!

19
00:01:04,993 --> 00:01:06,119
-Huh?
-Here, take it.

20
00:01:10,791 --> 00:01:14,961
Borrow it, return it,
let the sparks fly.

21
00:01:16,129 --> 00:01:18,882
-Mm-mm. No thanks.
-Why?

22
00:01:19,382 --> 00:01:21,635
Because then, you'll get drenched.

23
00:01:21,718 --> 00:01:24,054
Don't worry.
I live really close.

24
00:01:24,137 --> 00:01:25,639
Seriously!

25
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:28,767
I already owe you for breaking your phone.

26
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:31,103
I said it was okay. Just take it.

27
00:01:31,186 --> 00:01:33,897
You're going to
get sick out here like this.

28
00:01:35,315 --> 00:01:38,110
Well, I'm so slow,
I couldn't catch a cold.

29
00:01:38,193 --> 00:01:39,736
Your nose is running.

30
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:43,740
-And you were sneezing earlier.
-It's none of your business, okay?

31
00:01:44,324 --> 00:01:46,201
Stop being so stubborn.

32
00:01:46,785 --> 00:01:48,745
-Ugh, fine! Come to my place.
-Huh! What?

33
00:01:49,329 --> 00:01:52,582
I've got an extra umbrella
I was going to toss. You can take that.

34
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:54,251
Um, but…

35
00:01:56,086 --> 00:01:58,672
Listen, if you're worried about owing me…

36
00:01:58,755 --> 00:01:59,589
Hey…

37
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:01,633
…then just come on already.

38
00:02:01,716 --> 00:02:04,261
-Oh, okay.
-Let's go.

39
00:02:06,304 --> 00:02:07,764
Your hand…

40
00:02:13,645 --> 00:02:15,814
I'm sorry,
but you took forever to take it.

41
00:02:15,897 --> 00:02:18,692
Hey, wait up!
Now, you're getting wet.

42
00:02:20,026 --> 00:02:22,946
Sorry, you're just really tall.

43
00:02:27,075 --> 00:02:28,410
There! Problem solved.

44
00:02:29,077 --> 00:02:31,204
-Yeah.
-Come on then.

45
00:02:33,748 --> 00:02:35,125
This is every girl's dream.

46
00:02:35,792 --> 00:02:38,086
A hot guy sharing his umbrella

47
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:41,715
as you walk shoulder to shoulder
in the rain.

48
00:02:41,798 --> 00:02:44,676
Ugh, I will not give in!

49
00:04:18,311 --> 00:04:19,521
#2 IT'S TIME FOR CHILDREN
TO GO TO SLEEP

50
00:04:19,604 --> 00:04:20,772
Wait there a sec.

51
00:04:22,816 --> 00:04:25,986
He's hot and he lives alone.

52
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:31,324
No. I will not fall for this obvious trap.

53
00:04:31,408 --> 00:04:34,411
Just think about
your favorite game characters.

54
00:04:34,911 --> 00:04:36,454
Here.

55
00:04:36,538 --> 00:04:38,206
You should dry off

56
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:39,332
before you go.

57
00:04:39,416 --> 00:04:41,084
I've got this.

58
00:04:41,167 --> 00:04:43,336
Hot guy blurring filter.

59
00:04:47,674 --> 00:04:49,843
Yeah, that's better.

60
00:04:50,427 --> 00:04:51,511
Thanks.

61
00:04:52,053 --> 00:04:55,223
Not my business, but why
were you hiding in the park anyway?

62
00:04:55,307 --> 00:05:00,186
Hm, actually, there's this thing
at my place, a ro… ro…

63
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:02,856
-It's too terrifying. I can't even say it.
-Huh?

64
00:05:02,939 --> 00:05:03,982
Robber?

65
00:05:04,065 --> 00:05:06,609
Much worse, a roach!

66
00:05:07,193 --> 00:05:08,361
I said it.

67
00:05:09,404 --> 00:05:11,364
You let a bug chase you out of your house?

68
00:05:12,407 --> 00:05:15,243
It's not just "a bug", it was gigantic!

69
00:05:16,244 --> 00:05:20,665
My mom usually handles
this sort of thing or my cat,

70
00:05:20,749 --> 00:05:24,169
but my parents moved
overseas for work with the cat.

71
00:05:24,252 --> 00:05:27,255
First, the bug spray was empty,

72
00:05:27,339 --> 00:05:29,841
then, that thing came right for me,

73
00:05:29,924 --> 00:05:33,053
so I ran as fast as I could.

74
00:05:33,136 --> 00:05:37,849
I forgot my wallet and my phone.
Then it started raining.

75
00:05:39,434 --> 00:05:43,313
Ugh, it's the worst night ever.

76
00:05:45,106 --> 00:05:46,733
Your face…

77
00:05:46,816 --> 00:05:49,319
-Rude!
-I'm sorry.

78
00:05:49,402 --> 00:05:53,156
I thought he was the quiet type
who doesn't smile much but…

79
00:05:53,907 --> 00:05:55,742
That sounds like a nightmare.

80
00:05:59,037 --> 00:06:00,747
No!

81
00:06:01,706 --> 00:06:03,750
He broke down my barrier.

82
00:06:03,833 --> 00:06:05,627
You leave me no choice.

83
00:06:06,169 --> 00:06:08,505
Come forth, Momohiki!

84
00:06:14,886 --> 00:06:17,472
I guess that explains the mix-match shoes.

85
00:06:17,555 --> 00:06:20,058
It's working! Great job, Momohiki.

86
00:06:20,642 --> 00:06:23,103
-Want me to get rid of it?
-Huh?

87
00:06:24,145 --> 00:06:25,855
Want me to get rid of it for you?

88
00:06:25,939 --> 00:06:28,483
You know,
the thing that shall not be mentioned.

89
00:06:28,566 --> 00:06:29,567
For real?

90
00:06:30,819 --> 00:06:32,570
No, I'm in too deep already.

91
00:06:34,239 --> 00:06:36,116
No, I got this.

92
00:06:37,158 --> 00:06:40,036
Are you trying to avoid me or something?

93
00:06:40,578 --> 00:06:43,081
What? Of course not!

94
00:06:43,665 --> 00:06:47,001
If this is about
breaking my phone, don't worry about it.

95
00:06:47,085 --> 00:06:49,921
I was thinking about
getting a new one, anyway.

96
00:06:50,755 --> 00:06:51,589
Uh, um…

97
00:06:52,090 --> 00:06:55,427
I mean, seriously,
when you outright avoid me like that,

98
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:57,429
it makes me feel anxious.

99
00:06:57,512 --> 00:06:59,806
"Make me feel anxious"?

100
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:02,308
Well, if you don't want my help…

101
00:07:02,392 --> 00:07:06,771
No, really… I… need help.

102
00:07:07,355 --> 00:07:09,232
-All right, let's go.
-Huh…

103
00:07:12,277 --> 00:07:14,195
Here, it's cold. Wear this.

104
00:07:16,906 --> 00:07:20,577
How does he keep doing that?

105
00:07:27,167 --> 00:07:29,085
So, where is it?

106
00:07:29,711 --> 00:07:31,588
I saw it in the kitchen before.

107
00:07:35,175 --> 00:07:38,094
There's a hot guy in my house.

108
00:07:39,095 --> 00:07:40,346
I don't see it.

109
00:07:41,681 --> 00:07:44,058
This is way too ridiculous.

110
00:07:58,198 --> 00:08:01,576
It's right there! It's right there!

111
00:08:02,702 --> 00:08:07,123
My bad, just a lens cap.
Who the heck left that thing here?

112
00:08:08,791 --> 00:08:11,544
Did you just freak out over…

113
00:08:12,712 --> 00:08:15,465
How…

114
00:08:18,301 --> 00:08:20,887
How did we end up like this?

115
00:08:20,970 --> 00:08:24,140
Roaches are unseemly,
so instead, cake. You're welcome.

116
00:08:28,228 --> 00:08:31,147
Go get it! Go get it!

117
00:08:31,231 --> 00:08:32,649
That bastard!

118
00:08:40,323 --> 00:08:41,407
Piece of cake!

119
00:08:41,491 --> 00:08:44,035
Throw it away! Throw it away!

120
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:49,290
Thanks for helping
and sorry about stepping on you.

121
00:08:49,374 --> 00:08:51,543
Seriously, don't mention it.

122
00:08:51,626 --> 00:08:53,920
See you at school, Hoshino.

123
00:08:54,003 --> 00:08:56,548
Wait? How do you know my name?

124
00:08:57,298 --> 00:08:59,050
-Nameplate.
-Oh…

125
00:09:00,009 --> 00:09:02,053
Right.

126
00:09:02,136 --> 00:09:05,390
Tsukasa Kazuki. We go to the same school.

127
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:08,977
-Right. I'm Class 2.
-I'm Class 7.

128
00:09:09,561 --> 00:09:12,063
Do me a favor, don't avoid me anymore.

129
00:09:12,146 --> 00:09:14,232
Right.

130
00:09:14,816 --> 00:09:18,194
-Oh, can I at least wash your--
-No. Really. It's fine.

131
00:09:20,572 --> 00:09:24,075
Anyway, it might be a good idea
to take a nice warm bath.

132
00:09:24,158 --> 00:09:26,077
And be sure to bundle up.

133
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,287
Yes, dad.

134
00:09:28,288 --> 00:09:30,498
And you be sure
to eat something hot tonight.

135
00:09:30,582 --> 00:09:32,083
All right, Kazuki?

136
00:09:32,166 --> 00:09:33,918
Okay, mom.

137
00:09:34,002 --> 00:09:34,877
Later.

138
00:09:42,302 --> 00:09:45,972
-Guess I could run for it.
-Uh, well, this sucks.

139
00:09:46,055 --> 00:09:48,474
I'll be fine. See ya.

140
00:09:57,066 --> 00:09:59,861
Officials are expecting
the storm to last all night.

141
00:10:00,361 --> 00:10:04,866
A city-wide warning is in effect.
People have been asked to remain indoors,

142
00:10:04,949 --> 00:10:08,494
and avoid driving
in these severely dangerous conditions.

143
00:10:09,078 --> 00:10:11,080
Well, that's just great.

144
00:10:13,249 --> 00:10:15,251
A DREAM HOME

145
00:10:15,335 --> 00:10:18,963
This is my mom
and dad's dream house, their forever home.

146
00:10:19,047 --> 00:10:22,258
And they totally entrusted me
to take care of it while they're gone.

147
00:10:22,342 --> 00:10:26,095
Now, look at it!
Not only does this freaky weather

148
00:10:26,179 --> 00:10:28,431
crashed the tree
right into the front door,

149
00:10:28,514 --> 00:10:30,892
it also has me
stranded inside until it blows over.

150
00:10:31,434 --> 00:10:35,897
Stuck here with a super cute guy
standing right there in the living room.

151
00:10:36,814 --> 00:10:40,693
Wait a sec… Is this becoming…

152
00:10:40,777 --> 00:10:43,696
a sleepover situation?

153
00:10:44,864 --> 00:10:47,367
No way he can spend the night.

154
00:10:47,450 --> 00:10:49,285
We barely even know each other.

155
00:10:49,369 --> 00:10:51,245
Let's go, Anzu!

156
00:10:51,329 --> 00:10:53,373
-I am so not ready for this…
-Let's go, Anzu! Go!

157
00:10:53,456 --> 00:10:55,541
This was that thing's plan all along.

158
00:10:59,671 --> 00:11:01,130
Yeah, I'm hungry too.

159
00:11:01,756 --> 00:11:05,051
-I guess I'd better make some dinner.
-You're sure?

160
00:11:05,134 --> 00:11:07,595
Consider it a thank you
for getting rid of that bug.

161
00:11:09,639 --> 00:11:13,059
Problem is… what do I make?

162
00:11:13,685 --> 00:11:14,894
Let me see here.

163
00:11:14,977 --> 00:11:17,563
Maybe I can grill something
that's not overly fancy.

164
00:11:18,648 --> 00:11:20,566
A chance to earn girlfriend points.

165
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:34,747
This whole night!
You set all this up, didn't you?

166
00:11:34,831 --> 00:11:36,082
Well, duh.

167
00:11:37,166 --> 00:11:39,335
You even planted that bug!

168
00:11:39,419 --> 00:11:42,505
Sure, but thanks to me,
your evening is about to heat up.

169
00:11:42,588 --> 00:11:44,090
Ugh, this is all your fault.

170
00:11:44,173 --> 00:11:46,843
Not gonna lie, I was hoping
it would turn out like this.

171
00:11:48,094 --> 00:11:50,388
-I'm so scared.
-I've got you.

172
00:11:51,222 --> 00:11:53,599
I got to say,
I didn't think you'd tackle him.

173
00:11:54,183 --> 00:11:57,854
And that scream, like a bad word game.

174
00:11:57,937 --> 00:12:01,607
Shut up! I'll have you know
my scream is perfectly normal.

175
00:12:01,691 --> 00:12:02,859
I was pretty impressed

176
00:12:02,942 --> 00:12:05,069
that you were able to get him
on the floor so easily.

177
00:12:05,153 --> 00:12:07,613
That was a steamy moment
in the making, but no.

178
00:12:07,697 --> 00:12:10,366
Are you seriously judging me?

179
00:12:10,450 --> 00:12:11,617
Look!

180
00:12:11,701 --> 00:12:14,620
You're the one causing all this trouble.

181
00:12:14,704 --> 00:12:18,416
Don't fret.
I got everything under control.

182
00:12:18,499 --> 00:12:20,460
You call that "under control"?

183
00:12:20,543 --> 00:12:22,211
I can fix that. No problem.

184
00:12:22,712 --> 00:12:26,549
Chill up. It's time to blow him away
with your cooking skills.

185
00:12:26,632 --> 00:12:30,261
Remember, the way to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

186
00:12:30,344 --> 00:12:33,264
I only know how to cook stir-fry.

187
00:12:33,347 --> 00:12:36,434
Stir-fry? That's perfect!

188
00:12:36,517 --> 00:12:38,686
You can make Caprese sautée chicken?

189
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:42,273
Or blue crab with eggs and sauce?

190
00:12:42,356 --> 00:12:43,274
Get real!

191
00:12:45,234 --> 00:12:48,362
Why would I bother making
a good impression on this guy, anyway?

192
00:12:48,863 --> 00:12:50,823
MISO, SOY SAUCE

193
00:12:50,907 --> 00:12:52,867
Do you want miso or soy sauce?

194
00:12:54,368 --> 00:12:55,328
Miso.

195
00:12:55,411 --> 00:12:58,664
I handed you romance on a silver platter!

196
00:13:01,042 --> 00:13:02,251
Thanks for dinner.

197
00:13:04,337 --> 00:13:05,421
Oh, man.

198
00:13:07,632 --> 00:13:08,841
Hmm…

199
00:13:08,925 --> 00:13:13,304
I'm here to grant girls like you
who reject all opportunities of romance

200
00:13:13,387 --> 00:13:17,350
a chance to experience love
through this dating game.

201
00:13:18,184 --> 00:13:19,936
If that thing is causing all this,

202
00:13:20,019 --> 00:13:22,855
it's a safe bet
the storm won't let up till morning.

203
00:13:23,481 --> 00:13:26,234
You picked the wrong girl to mess with.

204
00:13:28,736 --> 00:13:30,947
You wanna play? Let's play.

205
00:13:33,282 --> 00:13:34,450
-Kazuki!
-Huh?

206
00:13:34,951 --> 00:13:37,078
Spend the night.

207
00:13:37,703 --> 00:13:39,831
Yeah, I think I'll pass on that.

208
00:13:41,916 --> 00:13:44,836
Do not fear.
There'll be no funny business.

209
00:13:45,711 --> 00:13:47,588
That's, uh, reassuring.

210
00:13:47,672 --> 00:13:51,384
Great! It's settled then.
Bath time! I'll fill up the tub.

211
00:13:51,467 --> 00:13:52,593
Huh?

212
00:13:52,677 --> 00:13:54,262
Uh…

213
00:14:01,811 --> 00:14:04,188
Here, these are my dad's,
but they should fit you.

214
00:14:04,272 --> 00:14:05,106
Thanks.

215
00:14:06,732 --> 00:14:08,234
You don't want to go first?

216
00:14:08,317 --> 00:14:10,778
Of course not. Guests always go first.

217
00:14:11,487 --> 00:14:12,321
Hm.

218
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:17,577
I knew you couldn't resist forever.

219
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:21,372
Now, you're spending the night together.
Next stop, romance!

220
00:14:26,419 --> 00:14:27,420
Hmm.

221
00:14:28,838 --> 00:14:30,548
So, I'll take the couch.

222
00:14:32,425 --> 00:14:34,260
This blanket should be warm enough.

223
00:14:35,219 --> 00:14:36,095
Huh?

224
00:14:40,641 --> 00:14:42,435
Thanks for the bath, Hoshino.

225
00:14:42,518 --> 00:14:46,063
No worries.
Oh, you didn't change your shirt?

226
00:14:46,647 --> 00:14:48,441
Yeah, not really my style.

227
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:51,569
It was the only one I could find for you.

228
00:14:51,652 --> 00:14:53,654
It would have been
kind of funny to see it on.

229
00:14:56,657 --> 00:14:58,659
That's much better!

230
00:15:03,706 --> 00:15:05,082
Ah…

231
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:06,584
-So lame!
-So lame!

232
00:15:06,667 --> 00:15:08,377
What's with the tucked-in shirt?

233
00:15:08,461 --> 00:15:10,504
You are not making this easy on me.

234
00:15:10,588 --> 00:15:12,590
You're the one who told me to bundle up.

235
00:15:13,799 --> 00:15:17,595
Consider it boy repellent. No chance
for romance when I'm dressed like this.

236
00:15:17,678 --> 00:15:19,722
Oh, no. Is she kidding…

237
00:15:19,805 --> 00:15:23,100
Abandoning all of her self-respect
to resist romance.

238
00:15:23,976 --> 00:15:26,812
So, Kazuki, wanna play a little game?

239
00:15:27,438 --> 00:15:28,356
What game?

240
00:15:29,231 --> 00:15:31,859
How about these?
I can't play them alone, you know.

241
00:15:32,610 --> 00:15:35,112
Okay. But I'm pretty good at these.

242
00:15:35,196 --> 00:15:38,324
Great! A worthy challenger.
This should be really fun.

243
00:15:41,953 --> 00:15:43,245
What?

244
00:15:49,835 --> 00:15:51,337
Uh, ugh…

245
00:15:53,547 --> 00:15:54,924
Ooh…

246
00:15:57,468 --> 00:16:01,138
-All right!
-Why can't I beat you?

247
00:16:02,431 --> 00:16:05,768
You're gonna have to put in a lot
more work if you wanna beat me at games.

248
00:16:06,352 --> 00:16:08,771
You don't have
to be a brat about it.

249
00:16:09,522 --> 00:16:10,564
-Ugh…
-Huh?

250
00:16:11,315 --> 00:16:12,775
I challenge you to a game of luck.

251
00:16:13,359 --> 00:16:15,361
Let's see how you do
without your strategies.

252
00:16:16,654 --> 00:16:20,074
Ha! Fine, but whoever loses
has to make lunch,

253
00:16:20,157 --> 00:16:22,284
and I'll take two desserts, thanks.

254
00:16:22,868 --> 00:16:25,204
-Slow down there.
-Game on, you're going down.

255
00:16:25,287 --> 00:16:27,039
I am gonna be a billionaire.

256
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,627
On that stormy night
at the Hoshino house,

257
00:16:31,711 --> 00:16:34,296
an epic board game battle began.

258
00:16:34,964 --> 00:16:39,385
Anzu, in her frumpiest PJ's,
completely ignoring a chance of romance.

259
00:16:39,468 --> 00:16:43,055
Kazuki with his best poker face,
seeking revenge.

260
00:16:43,139 --> 00:16:45,307
Each player oblivious to the situation.

261
00:16:45,391 --> 00:16:48,352
Each determined to be the winner!

262
00:16:50,438 --> 00:16:51,397
Hm.

263
00:16:53,899 --> 00:16:56,694
Hm, hm, hm, hm, hm…

264
00:16:56,777 --> 00:16:57,820
Hm?

265
00:16:57,903 --> 00:17:01,323
"You damaged a luxury car.
Pay 10,000 dollars."?

266
00:17:01,407 --> 00:17:02,992
I'm in debt already!

267
00:17:06,370 --> 00:17:07,830
Hm, hm…

268
00:17:07,913 --> 00:17:11,876
"You found an antique vase.
Collect the five-thousand-dollar reward."

269
00:17:11,959 --> 00:17:13,878
Who loses something like that?

270
00:17:14,462 --> 00:17:15,463
Grrr.

271
00:17:17,965 --> 00:17:19,925
"The gambling habit caught up to you.

272
00:17:20,009 --> 00:17:23,387
You lose all your money
at the races." Seriously?

273
00:17:29,185 --> 00:17:30,978
Hm, hm, hm…

274
00:17:31,062 --> 00:17:35,608
"You sold your macho men figures
to a collector. Earn 50,000 dollars."

275
00:17:36,192 --> 00:17:39,528
Come on! It's not fair!
You're landing on all the good stuff.

276
00:17:39,612 --> 00:17:42,615
Hey, don't blame me.
Luck's on my side tonight.

277
00:17:46,202 --> 00:17:48,662
So, that's how you wanna play?

278
00:17:49,705 --> 00:17:54,293
Grr. I will not lose!

279
00:17:55,211 --> 00:17:57,463
"You step in dog poop
and ruined your Jimmy Choo's.

280
00:17:57,546 --> 00:17:59,381
Replace them for 10,000 dollars."

281
00:17:59,465 --> 00:18:02,885
Who wears expensive shoes
like that to walk their dogs?

282
00:18:03,969 --> 00:18:06,889
"The shock of stepping in dog poop
makes you drop 10,000 dollars."

283
00:18:06,972 --> 00:18:08,891
No!

284
00:18:10,559 --> 00:18:11,393
Hm?

285
00:18:11,477 --> 00:18:14,855
"You dog, Pochi,
dug up Tokugawa's buried treasure.

286
00:18:14,939 --> 00:18:16,524
Collect one million dollars."

287
00:18:16,607 --> 00:18:19,652
-What?
-Good boy, Pochi.

288
00:18:20,903 --> 00:18:23,239
…two, three, four.

289
00:18:23,322 --> 00:18:26,325
"You step in dog poop
and ruined your Jimmy Choo's.

290
00:18:26,408 --> 00:18:29,662
Replace them for 10,000 dollars."
Not again!

291
00:18:30,246 --> 00:18:32,164
How many times
you're gonna step in poop?

292
00:18:32,248 --> 00:18:34,667
Yeah? Laugh it up! Go on!

293
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:38,671
Your dog's probably the one leaving
all that poop on my side of the street!

294
00:18:39,463 --> 00:18:41,423
Don't accuse my Pochi like that.

295
00:18:45,219 --> 00:18:47,138
Huh? Guess I won.

296
00:18:48,264 --> 00:18:49,890
What?

297
00:18:49,974 --> 00:18:53,144
Didn't have to put in that much more work
in order to beat you after all.

298
00:18:55,229 --> 00:18:57,314
Looks like Anzu lost. Too bad!

299
00:18:57,398 --> 00:18:59,692
I'll show you!

300
00:19:01,777 --> 00:19:03,696
This is such a drag.

301
00:19:03,779 --> 00:19:06,448
Why did I have to go
and open my big mouth?

302
00:19:07,074 --> 00:19:07,908
Huh?

303
00:19:08,701 --> 00:19:10,119
I thought I should help…

304
00:19:10,661 --> 00:19:13,080
since I lost the first game.

305
00:19:13,164 --> 00:19:15,416
Thank you!

306
00:19:15,499 --> 00:19:18,085
Feel free to use whatever
is in the fridge.

307
00:19:18,169 --> 00:19:19,461
You're the best!

308
00:19:20,796 --> 00:19:23,215
Come on, you have to
at least make something.

309
00:19:23,299 --> 00:19:25,009
I mean you are the loser.

310
00:19:25,676 --> 00:19:26,802
Don't rub it in.

311
00:19:34,310 --> 00:19:36,228
Do you always
put sugar in your eggs?

312
00:19:36,812 --> 00:19:39,315
Of course. That's how you make it.

313
00:19:40,566 --> 00:19:42,818
-Probably pineapple in your pork?
-Duh.

314
00:19:42,902 --> 00:19:45,070
-Potato apple salad?
-Delicious!

315
00:19:46,572 --> 00:19:48,240
You really are a weirdo.

316
00:19:48,824 --> 00:19:50,951
Weird or not,
I'm the one making the eggs,

317
00:19:51,035 --> 00:19:54,747
so I'll prepare them
how I like them, plain and simple.

318
00:20:07,218 --> 00:20:10,763
Huh? Is that supposed
to be scrambled eggs?

319
00:20:10,846 --> 00:20:13,807
For your information,
they don't always turn out this bad.

320
00:20:13,891 --> 00:20:15,809
Maybe you just need
a little more practice.

321
00:20:19,730 --> 00:20:21,774
Kazuki, these look delicious!

322
00:20:22,316 --> 00:20:23,859
Ah, mm.

323
00:20:23,943 --> 00:20:25,778
Mmm… Mm!

324
00:20:25,861 --> 00:20:29,198
These are crazy good!
Who knew you are such a pro.

325
00:20:29,281 --> 00:20:32,326
Well, I've been working part-time
in the kitchen of a local bar.

326
00:20:32,952 --> 00:20:35,663
Slow down.
Save some for lunch for tomorrow.

327
00:20:36,372 --> 00:20:37,623
What? I'm hungry.

328
00:20:37,706 --> 00:20:39,792
A girl can't live
on instant noodles alone.

329
00:20:39,875 --> 00:20:41,794
-I guess I should have made more.
-Hm…

330
00:20:41,877 --> 00:20:46,090
Or you can make some extra now,
so I can have some more tomorrow.

331
00:20:46,173 --> 00:20:47,299
Hm.

332
00:20:47,383 --> 00:20:49,551
-Don't be shy. Use the whole bag!
-Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

333
00:20:49,635 --> 00:20:51,303
Stop! That's too much.

334
00:20:51,387 --> 00:20:54,974
Looks so good!

335
00:20:55,057 --> 00:20:57,977
Oh, man! You even made octopus!

336
00:20:58,519 --> 00:21:00,521
You can't have homemade lunch
without octopus.

337
00:21:00,604 --> 00:21:01,438
Hmm…

338
00:21:07,111 --> 00:21:08,821
He's not at all
what I thought he was

339
00:21:08,904 --> 00:21:10,614
from my first impression.

340
00:21:20,457 --> 00:21:22,876
Everyone thinks he's this standoffish guy

341
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,462
but he's actually pretty easy to talk to.

342
00:21:25,546 --> 00:21:27,506
I feel like I could tell him anything.

343
00:21:29,258 --> 00:21:32,469
I am not developing feelings for him.
Not that he's interested.

344
00:21:32,553 --> 00:21:35,389
Besides, I haven't earned
any girlfriend points.

345
00:21:36,348 --> 00:21:38,892
How about I beat you
at a game of cards next?

346
00:21:38,976 --> 00:21:42,855
-Okay, just gotta use the restroom first.
-Sounds good.

347
00:21:44,481 --> 00:21:47,401
When did it get so late?
I'm not even tired.

348
00:21:48,193 --> 00:21:50,446
We can play Speed or Concentration.

349
00:21:50,529 --> 00:21:52,364
So many options.

350
00:21:52,448 --> 00:21:55,034
-What are you doing?
-Ugh, you again?

351
00:21:55,117 --> 00:21:58,787
Why are you wasting time
playing games like a bunch of little kids?

352
00:21:58,871 --> 00:22:03,208
Watch a rom-com, flirt.
Give in to the romance of it all.

353
00:22:03,292 --> 00:22:05,502
-No one asked you!
-Oh, sad.

354
00:22:05,586 --> 00:22:07,087
You couldn't even achieve the classic

355
00:22:07,171 --> 00:22:09,006
-run-into-each-other-in-the-bath scene.
-Grr.

356
00:22:09,590 --> 00:22:12,134
Try it and you and that wand
will get better acquainted.

357
00:22:12,801 --> 00:22:16,472
So, maybe I should have cast
that spell on you after all.

358
00:22:16,555 --> 00:22:18,265
Sorry to disappoint,

359
00:22:18,349 --> 00:22:20,476
but there is no chance this goes your way.

360
00:22:20,559 --> 00:22:23,187
Really?

361
00:22:24,396 --> 00:22:25,230
Ow!

362
00:22:30,486 --> 00:22:33,280
It's time for all good children
to go to sleep.

363
00:22:36,784 --> 00:22:38,452
What?

364
00:22:38,535 --> 00:22:41,205
Looks like she passed out. That was fast!

365
00:22:42,956 --> 00:22:46,835
Hoshino, if you're gonna sleep,
go to your room. Wake up!

366
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,837
Hm.

367
00:22:56,762 --> 00:22:57,930
Now, what'd I do?

368
00:22:58,430 --> 00:22:59,264
Hm?

369
00:22:59,890 --> 00:23:01,600
Shouldn't sleep with your glasses on.

370
00:23:09,191 --> 00:23:10,484
Mmm…

371
00:23:10,567 --> 00:23:13,362
Momohiki, I'll never let go, ever!

372
00:23:13,445 --> 00:23:15,823
Momohiki? Who the heck is that?

373
00:23:17,324 --> 00:23:18,951
What a grip!

374
00:23:20,327 --> 00:23:22,454
Jeez.

375
00:23:24,623 --> 00:23:26,792
I haven't had
that much fun in a long time.

376
00:23:38,762 --> 00:23:39,763
What a weirdo.

377
00:23:45,018 --> 00:23:46,562
A fanfare, please!

378
00:23:46,645 --> 00:23:48,689
And a big congratulations!

379
00:23:48,772 --> 00:23:50,816
Did you fall for my little trick?

380
00:23:50,899 --> 00:23:54,236
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

381
00:23:54,319 --> 00:23:57,865
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

382
00:23:57,948 --> 00:24:00,617
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

383
00:24:00,701 --> 00:24:02,995
Don't just let things be! Come on!

384
00:24:03,078 --> 00:24:05,664
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

385
00:24:05,747 --> 00:24:07,666
So I can make sure I get paid.

